WEBVTT

00:11:28.475 --> 00:11:30.477
with avian influenza, with Ebola,

00:11:30.519 --> 00:11:33.063
they knew the threat firsthand.

00:11:33.063 --> 00:11:36.066
They didn't need all of the data
in front of them to understand

00:11:36.108 --> 00:11:37.651
what a risk this posed.

00:11:37.693 --> 00:11:39.528
And they acted aggressively.

00:11:40.154 --> 00:11:42.239
And those countries
that had that experience

00:11:42.239 --> 00:11:45.325
really tackled this with the aggression
that was necessary.

00:11:45.367 --> 00:11:47.786
Far too many countries thought,

00:11:47.786 --> 00:11:49.246
"Not a problem for us.

00:11:49.288 --> 00:11:50.914
It's a problem over there.

00:11:50.914 --> 00:11:53.125
We've got a health system
that's very strong.

00:11:53.167 --> 00:11:54.501
We can handle it."

00:11:54.501 --> 00:11:57.379
But when you have an emerging new virus

00:11:57.421 --> 00:11:59.465
where the entire world is susceptible,

00:11:59.506 --> 00:12:01.341
you know very little about it --